The backend and the page are ported from the Notes app built into Kiro Crew
(https://github.com/kirodotdev/KiroCrew, Apache License 2.0); a few dashboard
helpers the page used are copied into ui/src/host/ from the same source.

The page bundle (ui/dist/index.mjs) is built from this repository's own
sources plus framer-motion 12.40.0, motion-dom 12.43.0 and motion-utils 12.39.0
(Motion Division Ltd, MIT License), highlight.js 11.11.1 (Ivan Sagalaev and
contributors, BSD 3-Clause License) and DOMPurify 3.4.17 (Cure53 and other
contributors, Apache License 2.0 or Mozilla Public License 2.0). The URL check
in ui/src/host/urlTransform.ts restates react-markdown 10.1.0's
defaultUrlTransform (Espen Hovlandsdal and Titus Wormer, MIT License).
React, lucide-react, TanStack Query and the Kiro Crew App SDK are provided by
the Kiro Crew dashboard at run time, and so is the Mermaid runtime the page
loads for diagrams. The backend uses aiohttp and PyYAML, which the Kiro Crew
gateway provides. The test suites install their pinned dependencies
(tests/requirements.txt, ui/package-lock.json), Kiro Crew among them, into a
test environment only.
